    "status": "DECLARED",
    "subject": "/root/augmented-lange-lerner/docs/Lange–Lerner_Model.pdf",
    "text": "Arrow [1951] provided a rigorous proof that every competitive equi- librium is a Pareto optimum (First Welfare Theorem) and that every Pareto optimum can be decentralised as a competitive equilibrium given an appropriate redistribution of endow- ments (Second Welfare Theorem).",
    "text_hash": "d5a63fc50e02bc85d0f4a8ed611f3708292de78f63f5928dc09ef7768759d370",
    "type": "theorem"
  },
  {
    "certs": [],
    "checkable": "machine",
    "falsifier": false,
    "id": "SRC-LANGE-LERNER-MODEL-e2b101c0-C002",
    "method": "deterministic",
    "provenance": "claim_ingest deterministic:quantifier",
    "risk": "exploratory",
    "section": "body",
    "source_id": "SRC-LANGE-LERNER-MODEL-e2b101c0",
    "status": "DECLARED",
    "subject": "/root/augmented-lange-lerner/docs/Lange–Lerner_Model.pdf",
    "text": "Ljungqvist and Sargent [2018] offer the most comprehensive treatment of recursive macroeconomic models, including the asset pricing equations and Euler conditions that the dynamic extension of the Lange–Lerner model must satisfy.",
    "text_hash": "55cda0680916aaddc8c4908cb466af84107ba485b20cda422fa6b96daae90f5a",
    "type": "theorem"
  },
