    "subject": "/root/augmented-lange-lerner/docs/Lange–Lerner_Model.pdf",
    "text": "There exists a feasible allocation (C            ⃗ 0 , I⃗ 0 ) such that, for all f and all t, \u0010         \u0011                       F X       \u0010          \u0011 ⃗ t(f ) > K K         ⃗ q⃗t(f ),0        and       L >           L q⃗t (f ),0 , f =1",
    "text_hash": "5b5e3b6f781d2ecfa2b77d05bba9585eabb4423d6b14b0d71214e5d4f2565987",
    "type": "number",
    "value": "1"
  },
  {
    "certs": [],
    "checkable": "machine",
    "falsifier": false,
    "id": "SRC-LANGE-LERNER-MODEL-e2b101c0-C030",
    "method": "deterministic",
    "provenance": "claim_ingest deterministic:quantifier",
    "risk": "exploratory",
    "section": "body",
    "source_id": "SRC-LANGE-LERNER-MODEL-e2b101c0",
    "status": "DECLARED",
    "subject": "/root/augmented-lange-lerner/docs/Lange–Lerner_Model.pdf",
    "text": "Suppose that X⃗ is concave in q⃗ and that ⃗ Z, ⃗                                             ⃗ −Z K, and L are convex in q⃗ (so that net output X    ⃗ is concave in q⃗), that household preferences uh are concave, and that β ∈ (0, 1) and δi ∈ (0, 1) for all i.",
    "text_hash": "958c4fe0a42da66fb4373aa493ba18cffdf1e687a3d28f5e033c0f3c051b0bd9",
    "type": "theorem"
  },
  {
    "certs": [],
    "checkable": "machine",
    "falsifier": false,
    "id": "SRC-LANGE-LERNER-MODEL-e2b101c0-C031",
    "method": "deterministic",
    "provenance": "claim_ingest deterministic:quantifier",
    "risk": "exploratory",
    "section": "body",
    "source_id": "SRC-LANGE-LERNER-MODEL-e2b101c0",
    "status": "DECLARED",
    "subject": "/root/augmented-lange-lerner/docs/Lange–Lerner_Model.pdf",
    "text": "The transversality condition is satisfied at the optimum, selecting the unique socially optimal path from among all paths satisfying the first-order conditions.",
    "text_hash": "67bf54301ac0911e86f99f6fb27dc3482a4814196491484205780deeb3211b1b",
    "type": "theorem"
  },
  {
    "certs": [],
    "checkable": "machine",
    "falsifier": false,
    "id": "SRC-LANGE-LERNER-MODEL-e2b101c0-C032",
    "method": "deterministic",
    "provenance": "claim_ingest deterministic:quantifier",
    "risk": "exploratory",
    "section": "body",
    "source_id": "SRC-LANGE-LERNER-MODEL-e2b101c0",
    "status": "DECLARED",
    "subject": "/root/augmented-lange-lerner/docs/Lange–Lerner_Model.pdf",
    "text": "Under the assumptions of Proposition 5.1, the optimal path satisfies lim β T ⃗λ⊤ ⃗ (f ) T KT +1 = 0 for all f.",
    "text_hash": "08e9fdb609b761a4c0681f04696f3fa534ff34ebf98509975cbe034b9147ce84",
    "type": "theorem"
  },
  {
    "certs": [],
    "checkable": "machine",
    "falsifier": false,
    "id": "SRC-LANGE-LERNER-MODEL-e2b101c0-C033",
    "method": "deterministic",
    "provenance": "claim_ingest deterministic:quantifier",
    "risk": "exploratory",
    "section": "body",
    "source_id": "SRC-LANGE-LERNER-MODEL-e2b101c0",
    "status": "DECLARED",
    "subject": "/root/augmented-lange-lerner/docs/Lange–Lerner_Model.pdf",
    "text": "Since V ∗ is bounded and the envelope condition holds at every t, the multiplier sequence {⃗μt + (I − ∆)⃗λt } is bounded: there exists M < ∞ such that ∥⃗μt + (I − ∆)⃗λt ∥ ≤ M for all t.",
    "text_hash": "a70b5c13c7aaba353b40be5edb665eb65bbf9c03b7a0c89c51108b778930c503",
    "type": "theorem"
  },
  {
    "certs": [],
    "checkable": "machine",
    "falsifier": true,
    "id": "SRC-LANGE-LERNER-MODEL-e2b101c0-C034",
    "method": "deterministic",
    "op": ">=",
    "provenance": "claim_ingest deterministic:ineq",
    "quantity": "c",
    "risk": "exploratory",
    "section": "body",
