    "subject": "/root/augmented-lange-lerner/docs/Lange–Lerner_Model.pdf",
    "text": "[1989, Theorem 4.15], this guarantees that the sequence problem and the recursive Bellman formulation are equivalent, and that the unique fixed point V ∗ of the Bellman operator selects the unique socially optimal path from among all paths satisfying the first-order conditions (B.1)–(B.3).",
    "text_hash": "82f56fa460a24ce62d89d1be6402990c0f99ad55336ff57ec04294d853d0130c",
    "type": "theorem"
  },
  {
    "certs": [],
