    "text": "(42) f =1",
    "text_hash": "5eac1ccd4e46026f19f596ccd8996113cb3b6d1fe39bff495e4b81e4e244d515",
    "type": "number",
    "value": "1"
  },
  {
    "certs": [],
    "checkable": "machine",
    "falsifier": false,
    "id": "SRC-LANGE-LERNER-MODEL-e2b101c0-C049",
    "method": "deterministic",
    "provenance": "claim_ingest deterministic:quantifier",
    "risk": "exploratory",
    "section": "body",
    "source_id": "SRC-LANGE-LERNER-MODEL-e2b101c0",
    "status": "DECLARED",
    "subject": "/root/augmented-lange-lerner/docs/Lange–Lerner_Model.pdf",
    "text": "In this formulation, policy improvement (f ) is a finite-dimensional optimization problem over the n diagonal entries of At and the n (f ) entries of ⃗bt , rather than an optimization performed separately at every point on a capital- state grid.",
    "text_hash": "58e949599d62380b29c7f16856f843012db7d65e6703786994672500b066573d",
    "type": "theorem"
  },
  {
    "certs": [],
    "checkable": "machine",
    "falsifier": false,
    "id": "SRC-LANGE-LERNER-MODEL-e2b101c0-C050",
    "method": "deterministic",
    "provenance": "claim_ingest deterministic:quantifier",
    "risk": "exploratory",
    "section": "body",
    "source_id": "SRC-LANGE-LERNER-MODEL-e2b101c0",
    "status": "DECLARED",
    "subject": "/root/augmented-lange-lerner/docs/Lange–Lerner_Model.pdf",
    "text": "The inner policy-iteration loop must also satisfy its own convergence criterion before the associated excess demand is communicated to the CPB.",
    "text_hash": "0bbc81e4c2c478c7a91c6ca1ef2ab32762752297d28038b27b709e0c00d708e7",
    "type": "theorem"
  },
  {
    "certs": [],
    "checkable": "machine",
    "falsifier": false,
    "id": "SRC-LANGE-LERNER-MODEL-e2b101c0-C051",
    "method": "deterministic",
    "provenance": "claim_ingest deterministic:quantifier",
    "risk": "exploratory",
    "section": "body",
    "source_id": "SRC-LANGE-LERNER-MODEL-e2b101c0",
    "status": "DECLARED",
    "subject": "/root/augmented-lange-lerner/docs/Lange–Lerner_Model.pdf",
    "text": "All household and firm sub-problems at a given outer iteration can be solved in paral- lel.",
    "text_hash": "b90f4360916f573f514a64ef625d66ce6e2125791fb2d1cf1616cca9ed73a1f5",
    "type": "theorem"
  },
  {
    "certs": [],
    "checkable": "machine",
    "falsifier": true,
    "id": "SRC-LANGE-LERNER-MODEL-e2b101c0-C052",
    "method": "deterministic",
    "op": "=",
    "provenance": "claim_ingest deterministic:num_eq",
    "quantity": "t",
    "risk": "exploratory",
    "section": "body",
    "source_id": "SRC-LANGE-LERNER-MODEL-e2b101c0",
    "status": "DECLARED",
    "subject": "/root/augmented-lange-lerner/docs/Lange–Lerner_Model.pdf",
    "text": "The social welfare function (14) then becomes                          \"∞                      # X X    H W = E0       βt          ⃗ h,t ) , wh uh (C                               (49) t=0    h=1",
    "text_hash": "0bc79c4769ff1906b0f686d8318538b10dce4b977a0c62ef1dd22200a2f7c98e",
    "type": "number",
    "value": "0"
  },
  {
