    "source_id": "SRC-LANGE-LERNER-MODEL-e2b101c0",
    "status": "DECLARED",
    "subject": "/root/augmented-lange-lerner/docs/Lange–Lerner_Model.pdf",
    "text": "The social welfare function (14) then becomes                          \"∞                      # X X    H W = E0       βt          ⃗ h,t ) , wh uh (C                               (49) t=0    h=1",
    "text_hash": "0bc79c4769ff1906b0f686d8318538b10dce4b977a0c62ef1dd22200a2f7c98e",
    "type": "number",
    "value": "1"
  },
  {
    "certs": [],
    "checkable": "machine",
    "falsifier": false,
    "id": "SRC-LANGE-LERNER-MODEL-e2b101c0-C054",
    "method": "deterministic",
    "provenance": "claim_ingest deterministic:quantifier",
    "risk": "exploratory",
    "section": "body",
    "source_id": "SRC-LANGE-LERNER-MODEL-e2b101c0",
    "status": "DECLARED",
    "subject": "/root/augmented-lange-lerner/docs/Lange–Lerner_Model.pdf",
    "text": "The CPB must then manage a complete set of Arrow–Debreu state-contingent prices, one for each good and each possible realisation of the uncertainty.",
    "text_hash": "1731d6c8acf1b2e8b14ef0257177a454b9a13bc7931b3c758ac691c8da181428",
    "type": "theorem"
  },
  {
    "certs": [],
    "checkable": "machine",
    "falsifier": true,
    "id": "SRC-LANGE-LERNER-MODEL-e2b101c0-C055",
    "method": "deterministic",
    "op": "=",
    "provenance": "claim_ingest deterministic:num_eq",
    "quantity": "f",
    "risk": "exploratory",
    "scope": "out_of_scope",
    "scope_reason": "control-chars",
    "section": "body",
    "source_id": "SRC-LANGE-LERNER-MODEL-e2b101c0",
    "status": "DECLARED",
    "subject": "/root/augmented-lange-lerner/docs/Lange–Lerner_Model.pdf",
    "text": "The labour supply constraint (17) is replaced by the economy-wide time endowment constraint XF     \u0010 \u0011 X      H (f ) L q⃗t    ≤     (1 − ℓh,t ),                            (51) f =1             h=1",
    "text_hash": "237852dbeb7739cb7eaf085a63ed3c79dbe561211626de0f3b30c81793ccecb1",
    "type": "number",
    "value": "1"
  },
  {
    "certs": [],
    "checkable": "machine",
    "falsifier": true,
    "id": "SRC-LANGE-LERNER-MODEL-e2b101c0-C056",
    "method": "deterministic",
    "op": "=",
    "provenance": "claim_ingest deterministic:num_eq",
    "quantity": "h",
    "risk": "exploratory",
    "scope": "out_of_scope",
    "scope_reason": "control-chars",
    "section": "body",
    "source_id": "SRC-LANGE-LERNER-MODEL-e2b101c0",
    "status": "DECLARED",
    "subject": "/root/augmented-lange-lerner/docs/Lange–Lerner_Model.pdf",
    "text": "The labour supply constraint (17) is replaced by the economy-wide time endowment constraint XF     \u0010 \u0011 X      H (f ) L q⃗t    ≤     (1 − ℓh,t ),                            (51) f =1             h=1",
    "text_hash": "237852dbeb7739cb7eaf085a63ed3c79dbe561211626de0f3b30c81793ccecb1",
    "type": "number",
    "value": "1"
  },
  {
    "certs": [],
    "checkable": "machine",
    "falsifier": false,
    "id": "SRC-LANGE-LERNER-MODEL-e2b101c0-C057",
    "method": "deterministic",
    "provenance": "claim_ingest deterministic:quantifier",
    "risk": "exploratory",
    "section": "body",
    "source_id": "SRC-LANGE-LERNER-MODEL-e2b101c0",
    "status": "DECLARED",
    "subject": "/root/augmented-lange-lerner/docs/Lange–Lerner_Model.pdf",
    "text": "The consumer sub-problem (22) acquires an additional first-order condition equating the marginal rate of substitution between consumption and leisure to the real wage, and the master problem (34) must additionally clear the endogenous labour supply through the wage νt .",
    "text_hash": "d6efce7e4bde442f6001969ab86cbb72caf4f3ffcc555950174c517093dc3f06",
    "type": "theorem"
  },
  {
    "certs": [],
    "checkable": "machine",
    "falsifier": true,
    "id": "SRC-LANGE-LERNER-MODEL-e2b101c0-C058",
    "method": "deterministic",
    "op": "=",
    "provenance": "claim_ingest deterministic:num_eq",
    "quantity": "f",
    "risk": "exploratory",
    "scope": "out_of_scope",
    "scope_reason": "control-chars",
    "section": "body",
    "source_id": "SRC-LANGE-LERNER-MODEL-e2b101c0",
    "status": "DECLARED",
    "subject": "/root/augmented-lange-lerner/docs/Lange–Lerner_Model.pdf",
    "text": "The market-clearing condition (15) is modified to include net exports N⃗X t , so that F h \u0010 X           \u0011     \u0010 \u0011            i XH ⃗   (f )     ⃗   (f )   ⃗(f )      ⃗ h,t + N⃗X t , X q⃗t      − Z q⃗t    − It     =   C                                      (52) f =1                                    h=1",
    "text_hash": "ddb5e2c6ad9bd09a9a1ca3fa88aaed85518f314094ff575764cc7d55f27982a8",
    "type": "number",
    "value": "1"
  },
  {
    "certs": [],
    "checkable": "machine",
    "falsifier": true,
    "id": "SRC-LANGE-LERNER-MODEL-e2b101c0-C059",
    "method": "deterministic",
    "op": "=",
    "provenance": "claim_ingest deterministic:num_eq",
    "quantity": "h",
    "risk": "exploratory",
    "scope": "out_of_scope",
    "scope_reason": "control-chars",
    "section": "body",
    "source_id": "SRC-LANGE-LERNER-MODEL-e2b101c0",
    "status": "DECLARED",
    "subject": "/root/augmented-lange-lerner/docs/Lange–Lerner_Model.pdf",
    "text": "The market-clearing condition (15) is modified to include net exports N⃗X t , so that F h \u0010 X           \u0011     \u0010 \u0011            i XH ⃗   (f )     ⃗   (f )   ⃗(f )      ⃗ h,t + N⃗X t , X q⃗t      − Z q⃗t    − It     =   C                                      (52) f =1                                    h=1",
    "text_hash": "ddb5e2c6ad9bd09a9a1ca3fa88aaed85518f314094ff575764cc7d55f27982a8",
    "type": "number",
    "value": "1"
  },
  {
    "certs": [],
    "checkable": "machine",
    "falsifier": true,
    "id": "SRC-LANGE-LERNER-MODEL-e2b101c0-C060",
    "method": "deterministic",
    "op": "=",
    "provenance": "claim_ingest deterministic:num_eq",
    "quantity": "t",
    "risk": "exploratory",
    "section": "body",
    "source_id": "SRC-LANGE-LERNER-MODEL-e2b101c0",
    "status": "DECLARED",
    "subject": "/root/augmented-lange-lerner/docs/Lange–Lerner_Model.pdf",
    "text": "subject to the trade balance condition p⃗∗⊤ ⃗               ⃗∗t denotes the exogenously given t N X t = 0, where p vector of world prices.",
    "text_hash": "440e0575d80ec8248d33b5b2f147a1485c2bf26b978bfd3ee0a9001a2161e82f",
    "type": "number",
    "value": "0"
  },
  {
    "certs": [],
    "checkable": "machine",
    "falsifier": false,
    "id": "SRC-LANGE-LERNER-MODEL-e2b101c0-C061",
    "method": "deterministic",
    "provenance": "claim_ingest deterministic:quantifier",
    "risk": "exploratory",
    "section": "body",
    "source_id": "SRC-LANGE-LERNER-MODEL-e2b101c0",
    "status": "DECLARED",
    "subject": "/root/augmented-lange-lerner/docs/Lange–Lerner_Model.pdf",
    "text": "The CPB in the open economy must additionally determine the quantities of goods exchanged with the rest of the world, and the master problem (34) is augmented by the trade balance as a further coupling constraint.",
    "text_hash": "99de924acab2077664ee0e6fe4d73a01d80ea45791ae646815e0c9cc4b5a8ba1",
    "type": "theorem"
  },
  {
    "certs": [],
    "checkable": "machine",
    "falsifier": false,
    "id": "SRC-LANGE-LERNER-MODEL-e2b101c0-C062",
    "method": "deterministic",
    "negated": true,
    "provenance": "claim_ingest deterministic:quantifier",
    "risk": "exploratory",
    "section": "body",
    "source_id": "SRC-LANGE-LERNER-MODEL-e2b101c0",
    "status": "DECLARED",
    "subject": "/root/augmented-lange-lerner/docs/Lange–Lerner_Model.pdf",
    "text": "In this case, the price-iteration mechanism of the master problem (34) cannot in general recover the social optimum, since no price system can decentralise an al- location that lies outside the convex hull of the production possibility set.",
    "text_hash": "cc2f9bd29d53f765117acf4daf9fcae4d14c69e518c49ae85c964a9133a95809",
    "type": "theorem"
  },
  {
    "certs": [],
    "checkable": "machine",
    "falsifier": false,
    "id": "SRC-LANGE-LERNER-MODEL-e2b101c0-C063",
    "method": "deterministic",
    "provenance": "claim_ingest deterministic:quantifier",
    "refs": [
      "eq:41-42"
    ],
    "risk": "exploratory",
    "section": "body",
    "source_id": "SRC-LANGE-LERNER-MODEL-e2b101c0",
    "status": "DECLARED",
    "subject": "/root/augmented-lange-lerner/docs/Lange–Lerner_Model.pdf",
    "text": "The planning mechanism proposed in this paper satisfies the informational requirements identified by Malinvaud [1967]: the only information the Central Planning Board must broadcast to firms and house- holds is the price system (⃗λt , νt ), and the only information that firms and households must communicate to the CPB is their excess demands (41)–(42).",
    "text_hash": "e7ce68f70adc88a0268ac7819fcd6bee19c5718f82211481d89349354ecb6921",
    "type": "theorem"
  },
  {
    "certs": [],
    "checkable": "machine",
    "falsifier": false,
    "id": "SRC-LANGE-LERNER-MODEL-e2b101c0-C064",
    "method": "deterministic",
    "negated": true,
    "provenance": "claim_ingest deterministic:quantifier",
    "risk": "exploratory",
    "section": "body",
    "source_id": "SRC-LANGE-LERNER-MODEL-e2b101c0",
    "status": "DECLARED",
    "subject": "/root/augmented-lange-lerner/docs/Lange–Lerner_Model.pdf",
    "text": "The nesting of a globally convergent inner loop within an outer loop whose convergence depends on convexity means that the algorithm inherits the limitations of the tâtonnement procedure: it is a reliable computational method for convex economies, but cannot be relied upon in the presence of non-convexities without additional modifications such as random restarts or global search methods.",
    "text_hash": "97259736b23c24b10a8b276f11e49eb54f069fe39dd25154e15411d10bac2a23",
    "type": "theorem"
  },
  {
    "certs": [],
    "checkable": "machine",
    "falsifier": false,
    "id": "SRC-LANGE-LERNER-MODEL-e2b101c0-C065",
    "method": "deterministic",
    "negated": true,
    "provenance": "claim_ingest deterministic:quantifier",
    "risk": "exploratory",
    "section": "body",
    "source_id": "SRC-LANGE-LERNER-MODEL-e2b101c0",
    "status": "DECLARED",
    "subject": "/root/augmented-lange-lerner/docs/Lange–Lerner_Model.pdf",
    "text": "The computational interpretation is therefore closely related to the original insight of Lange and Lerner: the planning authority need not directly determine every allocation, but can instead coordinate decentralised decisions through a system of prices and associated shadow values.",
    "text_hash": "e27ea8ede6de348c2e9ce18660848af0c059d4ca662efb0d85ea588cc8fbe0d9",
    "type": "theorem"
  },
  {
    "certs": [],
    "checkable": "machine",
    "falsifier": false,
    "id": "SRC-LANGE-LERNER-MODEL-e2b101c0-C066",
    "method": "agent",
    "provenance": "claim_ingest agent",
    "risk": "exploratory",
    "section": "abstract",
    "source_id": "SRC-LANGE-LERNER-MODEL-e2b101c0",
    "status": "DECLARED",
    "subject": "/root/augmented-lange-lerner/docs/Lange–Lerner_Model.pdf",
    "text": "The classical Lange-Lerner model is Pareto efficient in the static formulation of the Arrow-Debreu model.",
    "text_hash": "29aee577fa324f34a080de1e79209035c09b127acf809b45337e46f591df7df9",
    "type": "theorem"
  },
  {
    "certs": [],
    "checkable": "machine",
    "falsifier": false,
    "id": "SRC-LANGE-LERNER-MODEL-e2b101c0-C067",
    "method": "agent",
    "provenance": "claim_ingest agent",
    "risk": "exploratory",
    "section": "abstract",
    "source_id": "SRC-LANGE-LERNER-MODEL-e2b101c0",
    "status": "DECLARED",
    "subject": "/root/augmented-lange-lerner/docs/Lange–Lerner_Model.pdf",
    "text": "The Lange-Lerner model fails to remain efficient in its dynamic formulation.",
    "text_hash": "a4574c19012e6b4761a2439130a84ed05f377f8b59a28cd283076ab3e7b7b940",
    "type": "theorem"
  },
  {
    "certs": [],
    "checkable": "machine",
    "falsifier": false,
    "id": "SRC-LANGE-LERNER-MODEL-e2b101c0-C068",
    "method": "agent",
    "provenance": "claim_ingest agent",
    "risk": "exploratory",
    "section": "abstract",
    "source_id": "SRC-LANGE-LERNER-MODEL-e2b101c0",
    "status": "DECLARED",
    "subject": "/root/augmented-lange-lerner/docs/Lange–Lerner_Model.pdf",
    "text": "The modified model achieves Pareto efficiency in the dynamic Arrow-Debreu framework.",
    "text_hash": "d866027b751776e232c619011bf414b3defea62c3b7947042c59ff65698bebd0",
    "type": "theorem"
  }
]
